# The completed naive cotangent complex of an adic, topologically finite type arrow

Let `A → B` be an arrow of `WAdm^{adic*}` which is adic and topologically of finite type.
Writing `B = A{x₁, …, x_r} / J` as a quotient of a restricted power series ring by a closed
ideal, the completed naive cotangent complex is the two-term complex

```
NL^∧_{B/A} = (J / J² → ⨁ i, B dxᵢ)
```

in degrees `-1` and `0`, whose differential sends the class of `g ∈ J` to the tuple of its
formal partial derivatives. It is well defined up to unique isomorphism in the homotopy
category `K(B)`. When `A` is Noetherian and `I ⊆ A` is an ideal of definition, this
construction reproduces the complex of Equation 0AJR for `(A, I)`; in particular that complex
does not depend on the choice of `I`.

## Main definitions

* `Rig.RestrictedPowerSeriesPresentation` records a presentation of `B` as a topological
  `A`-algebra quotient of a restricted power series ring by a closed ideal.
* `Rig.RestrictedNaiveCotangentComplex` is the complex attached to such a presentation, with
  its formal partial derivatives and its differential pinned by the source's formula.
* `Rig.RestrictedPresentationComparison` is a morphism of presentations together with the map
  of complexes it induces, pinned on conormal classes and on the free generators.
* `Rig.NoetherianPresentationComparison` is the identification, for an ideal of definition `I`
  of a Noetherian `A`, of this complex with the one of Equation 0AJR.

## Main results

* `Rig.nonempty_restrictedNaiveCotangentComplex` constructs the complex for any presentation,
  and `Rig.restrictedNaiveCotangentComplex` is the complex it produces.
* `Rig.nonempty_restrictedPowerSeriesPresentation`: an adic arrow of topological finite type
  between adic rings with finitely generated ideals of definition has a presentation.
* `Rig.exists_restrictedPresentationComparison` and
  `Rig.homotopy_of_restrictedPresentationComparison` are well-definedness up to *unique*
  isomorphism in `K(B)`.
* `Rig.exists_noetherianPresentationComparison` is the agreement with Equation 0AJR.
* `Rig.nonempty_homotopyEquiv_of_idealOfDefinition` is the independence of the complex of
  Equation 0AJR from the chosen ideal of definition.

## Implementation notes

The restricted power series ring is `TopologicalRing.RestrictedPowerSeries`, the completion of
the polynomial ring for the topology generated by the open ideals of the coefficient ring. It
is the ring occurring in condition (7) of Tag 0GBW, which is the hypothesis of the source, and
it depends only on the topology of `A` and not on a choice of ideal of definition — which is
what makes the final claim of the source a consequence of the others rather than a separate
assumption. The other restricted power series ring in the library, `RestrictedPowerSeries`, is
indexed by an ideal and is therefore not available for that purpose.

No Noetherian hypothesis is imposed on the construction or on its presentation independence,
as the source imposes none; `IsNoetherianRing A` appears only in the last two results, where
the source introduces it. The construction is also stated for a merely linearly topologized
`A`, since the adic hypotheses of the source are what guarantee that a presentation exists,
not what makes the complex well defined once one is given.

Formal partial derivatives are not defined separately but are pinned inside
`RestrictedNaiveCotangentComplex` as the unique continuous derivations extending the
polynomial partial derivatives, exactly as in `Rig.CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex`;
`RestrictedNaiveCotangentComplex.ext` proves that this determines all of the data, so the
structure is not an unconstrained existential. The conormal module and the free module may lie
in different universes, so the cochain complex uses their universe lifts, as in Tag 0AJR.

Because the structure pins all of its own data it is a subsingleton, which is what
`RestrictedNaiveCotangentComplex.subsingleton` records. The construction of the source is
therefore stated as the inhabitedness claim `nonempty_restrictedNaiveCotangentComplex`, and
`restrictedNaiveCotangentComplex` is a definition with a body: the unique inhabitant. Had the
definition itself been left as a specification hole, it would have asserted nothing about which
complex is meant.

